## Induction Heating sample: half-torus coil (native torus + webcut)
## Required labels: source, sink (sidesets on cut faces)
## Optional labels: workpiece, air
##
## Creates a half-torus coil by webcut of native ACIS torus.
## Native 'create torus' produces a single toroidal surface that
## passes p-convergence cleanly (unlike sweep, which splits into
## upper/lower halves causing ACIS projection issues).
##
## Usage: Solve -> Radia-NGSolve -> Induction Heating

reset

# Create torus coil (R_major=0.11 m, R_minor=0.01 m)
create torus major radius 0.11 minor radius 0.01

# Cut with YZ plane to create terminal faces
webcut volume 1 with plane xplane noimprint nomerge

# Delete one half to get a C-shape (half-torus)
delete volume 2

# Mesh
volume 1 scheme tetmesh
volume 1 size auto factor 5
mesh volume 1

# Material block
block 1 add volume 1
block 1 name "coil"

# Terminal faces (created by webcut)
sideset 1 add surface 2
sideset 1 name "source"
sideset 2 add surface 3
sideset 2 name "sink"
